            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for a verdict, then the Kannada for a punishment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ರಾಜ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ರಾಜ — rāja — \"a king\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾನು ರಾಜ ಆಗಿದ್ದರೆ ಎಲ್ಲರಿಗೂ ಮನೆ ಕಟ್ಟಿಸುತ್ತಿದ್ದೆ. nānu rāja āgiddare ellarigū mane kaṭṭisuttidde. If I were king, I would have houses built for everyone."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ರಾಜರು, rājaru."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The land a king rules is his ರಾಜ್ಯ, and he lives in an ಅರಮನೆ, a palace."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ರಾಜ (rāja) is borrowed from Sanskrit rājan, \"a chieftain, a king\" (CDIAL 10679), in its compound form rāja."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
