          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ರಾಣಿ — rāṇi — \"a queen\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ರಾಣಿ ಅರಮನೆಯ ತೋಟದಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆಯುತ್ತಿದ್ದಳು. rāṇi aramaneya tōṭadalli naḍeyuttiddaḷu. The queen was walking in the palace garden."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ರಾಣಿಯರು, rāṇiyaru."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ರಾಣಿ (rāṇi) goes back to Sanskrit rājñī, \"a queen\" (CDIAL 10692), the feminine of rājan; the spoken languages of the north smoothed it to rāṇī, and Kannada took that form."
            }
          ]
        },
