          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಳು — āḷu — \"to reign; to rule\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆ ರಾಜ ನಲವತ್ತು ವರ್ಷ ಈ ನಾಡನ್ನು ಆಳಿದನು. ā rāja nalavattu varṣa ī nāḍannu āḷidanu. That king ruled this land for forty years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಆಳಿದೆ, āḷide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is ruled takes -ಅನ್ನು. A different ಆಳು (āḷu), a noun, means a servant or a worker."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಳು (āḷu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 5157 lists Kannada āḷ, \"to possess, govern, rule\", beside Tamil āḷ, \"to rule, reign over\"."
            }
          ]
        },
